    "fullName": "Joshua Niño C. Angeles",
    "headline": "Computer Engineering Student",
    "tagline": "I connect software logic with physical hardware — from embedded firmware to 3D mechanical design.",
    "shortBio": "Analytical computer engineering student with a multidisciplinary foundation spanning embedded systems programming, CAD mechanical design, and circuit prototyping. Siemens Solid Edge Certified Mechanical Associate (SSECMA) with formal Java programming credentials — a rare ability to integrate software logic with physical hardware engineering and 3D modeling.",
    "longBio": "I'm currently finishing my BS in Computer Engineering at STI Ortigas-Cainta College (2023–present). My thesis is an Arduino-based automated pet food weighing vending machine — receipt printing with stock monitoring — which combines firmware, circuit design, and mechanical assembly in one build.\n\nI started in the STEM strand, where our research on an automatic trash can decomposer turned food waste into fertilizer and won awards at SHS EXPO 2023. Since then I've built a 6-DOF robotic arm, a domestic cleaning robot prototype, and a solar-powered mobile charging system. I'm looking for an internship where I can work close to the metal — embedded systems, hardware prototyping, or mechanical design.",
    "location": "Cainta, Rizal, Philippines",
